      "value": "@{58c6da1b23f8d63e1401d381|full_name}: A way to do it could be like this:\nCurrently there's 2 poly limits. The soft limit at 10k and the hard limit at 20k. It could work by adding a LOD requirement for avatars over say… 12k. So for anything over that, users would then have to implement the LOD meshes themselves, however they want to do that. Simple decimation, edge loop removal, whatever.\n\nAlong with that there could also be a 'autogenerate LOD meshes' with a warning that there is no certainty of quality.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
